---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ScriptList from "../components/ScriptList.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <main>
    <section class="intro">
      <h1>User scripts and Tampermonkey</h1>
      <p>
        A user script is a program for modifying web pages. On this page you
        will find a collection of such programs written in JavaScript, that I
        have found useful in my work here at the <a
          href="https://www.uia.no/english/index.html"
          target="_blank">University of Agder (UiA)</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        In order to use a user script, a browser extension is required. The
        scripts here are written using the extension Tampermonkey. You can <a
          href="https://www.tampermonkey.net/"
          target="_blank">visit the Tampermonkey home page</a
        > where you will find instructions on how to install it for your browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        In order to install a script, first locate it in the list below. Then
        you click the title to open the page for that script. Once you are on
        the page, you can read more about it, and there will also be a link at
        the top to install it. When you click the install link, you will
        automatically be prompted to install it. Just confirm the installation,
        and you're ready to go!
      </p>
    </section>

    <ScriptList />
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  main {
    margin: 2rem;
  }

  .intro{
	max-width: 800px;
	margin: 0 auto;
  }
</style>
